                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="902-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>MXL V63M</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The V63M is a transformerless large-diaphragm condenser with a fixed cardioid pickup pattern. Part of MXL&#8217;s &#8220;900 Series,&#8221; it is OEM&#8217;d by MXL for Guitar Center and its various retail outlets, including Musician&#8217;s Friend, Music 123, and Woodwind &amp; Brasswind.</p><p>The capsule has an outside diameter of 32mm, with a 6-micron diaphragm. The Mylar on the rear of the capsule is clear, as is often the case on Cardioid-only condensers.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/mxl/v63m-pcb.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/mxl/v63m-pcb-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="V63M" width="133" /></a>The impedance circuitry is transformerless. This specific circuit design is commonly referred to as the &#8220;Schoeps circuit,&#8221; named for the German manufacturer that pioneered it. The same circuit &#8212; in fact, identical circuit boards &#8212; can be found in numerous other MXL mics, including the MCA SP-1, MXL V57, MXL V250, and MXL 2006.</p><p>The V63M and SP-1 differ in two ways: the SP-1 uses a small-diaphragm capsule, and uses a lighter weight (thinner) body sleeve. The V63M and 2006 differ only in the shape of the body and headbasket; internally, they share the same circuit and capsule.</p><p>The V63M&#8217;s self-noise is rated at 20dBA, making this the noisiest of MXL&#8217;s large-diapragm FET microphones (along with the multipattern <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/4000">MXL 4000</a>, another 900-series mic). </p><p>The performance of this microphone can be substantially improved through a variety of aftermarket modifications. See the sidebar for commercial mod kids and upgrade options.</p><p>The V63M ships with a ring mount (MXL p/n MT-001). Some retailers bundle it with an elastic shockmount; the mic is compatible with the MXL-57, USM-001, and USM-002 shockmounts.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/V63M">MXL V63M</a></p>
